" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M6 2L3 6v14a2 2 0 002 2h14a2 2 0 002-2V6l-3-4z\"></path><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"6\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"6\"></line><path d=\"M16 10a4 4 0 01-8 0\"></path></svg></button><button class=\"flex lg:hidden h-9 w-9 items-center justify-center rounded-button text-foreground-muted transition-colors duration-150 hover:bg-surface-hover cursor-pointer\" aria-label=\"Toggle menu\" aria-expanded=\"false\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><line x1=\"4\" y1=\"7\" x2=\"20\" y2=\"7\"></line><line x1=\"4\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"20\" y2=\"12\"></line><line x1=\"4\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"20\" y2=\"17\"></line></svg></button></div></div></header><div class=\"w-full border-b border-border/40 bg-surface-elevated/80 dark:bg-surface-elevated/40 backdrop-blur-sm relative z-40\" id=\"global-search-bar\"><div class=\"relative mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6\"><div class=\"flex items-center h-11 gap-3\"><svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"text-brand-500/60 dark:text-brand-400/50 shrink-0\"><circle cx=\"11\" cy=\"11\" r=\"8\"></circle><line x1=\"21\" y1=\"21\" x2=\"16.65\" y2=\"16.65\"></line></svg><input type=\"text\" placeholder=\"Search products, certificates, articles, or batch numbers...\" class=\"flex-1 bg-transparent text-[13px] text-foreground placeholder:text-foreground-muted/50 outline-none tracking-wide\" autocomplete=\"off\" value=\"\"></div></div></div><main class=\"no-overflow-x flex-1\"><div class=\"page-enter\"><section class=\"pt-6 sm:pt-8 pb-20 text-readable\"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6\"><p class=\"font-mono text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 accent-glow mb-3\">Works on Any Vendor</p><h1 class=\"text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-foreground\">Peptide COA Verification</h1><div class=\"mt-4 w-12 h-px bg-brand-300/50 dark:bg-border-strong\"></div><p class=\"mt-6 text-[15px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">Every peptide vendor in Canada claims purity. Almost none of those claims can be independently checked. The four steps below work against any supplier’s certificate — including ours. We can afford to publish this checklist because we pass it; use it on everyone.</p><ol class=\"mt-10 space-y-8\"><li class=\"flex gap-5\"><span class=\"flex items-center justify-center h-8 w-8 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500/10 dark:bg-brand-500/15 border border-brand-300/30 dark:border-brand-500/20 font-mono text-[13px] font-semibold text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400\">1</span><div><h2 class=\"text-[15px] font-medium text-foreground\">Match the lot code on the vial to the certificate</h2><p class=\"mt-2 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">A certificate without a lot code match proves nothing about your vial. The code printed on the label must appear on the certificate itself — not just on the product page. If a vendor publishes one undated “example COA” for a product, that is a brochure, not verification.</p></div></li><li class=\"flex gap-5\"><span class=\"flex items-center justify-center h-8 w-8 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500/10 dark:bg-brand-500/15 border border-brand-300/30 dark:border-brand-500/20 font-mono text-[13px] font-semibold text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400\">2</span><div><h2 class=\"text-[15px] font-medium text-foreground\">Open the certificate on the laboratory’s own portal</h2><p class=\"mt-2 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">A PDF or image can be edited. The test is whether the issuing lab hosts the same result on its own database — Janoshik Analytical, for example, runs a public verification portal where any test can be looked up by its code. A certificate that exists only on the vendor’s server is a weaker claim by definition.</p></div></li><li class=\"flex gap-5\"><span class=\"flex items-center justify-center h-8 w-8 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500/10 dark:bg-brand-500/15 border border-brand-300/30 dark:border-brand-500/20 font-mono text-[13px] font-semibold text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400\">3</span><div><h2 class=\"text-[15px] font-medium text-foreground\">Look for measured content, not just purity</h2><p class=\"mt-2 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">Purity says what fraction of the material is the target compound; it says nothing about how much material is in the vial. A 99.8% pure vial can be 30% underfilled. A complete certificate reports the measured mass against the label. Most vendors omit this number — ask why.</p></div></li><li class=\"flex gap-5\"><span class=\"flex items-center justify-center h-8 w-8 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500/10 dark:bg-brand-500/15 border border-brand-300/30 dark:border-brand-500/20 font-mono text-[13px] font-semibold text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400\">4</span><div><h2 class=\"text-[15px] font-medium text-foreground\">Check the test date against the batch</h2><p class=\"mt-2 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">The test date should sit shortly after the production date and before the sale. A certificate dated long before the batch it supposedly covers, or reused across multiple batches, is one of the classic red flags — our guide to spotting fakes covers the full list.</p></div></li></ol><div class=\"mt-12 glass rounded-card border border-border/60 p-6\"><h2 class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-foreground\">Verify an Eppix Labs batch now</h2><p class=\"mt-2 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">Enter the lot code printed on your vial and get the full analytical record — purity, measured content, fill accuracy — plus the issuing laboratory’s own verification link.</p><div class=\"mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-[14px]\"><a class=\"text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline\" href=\"/verify\">Open the batch verifier →</a><a class=\"text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline\" href=\"/certificates-of-analysis\">Browse the COA library →</a></div></div><h2 class=\"mt-12 text-xl font-semibold text-foreground\">Go deeper</h2><ul class=\"mt-4 space-y-2.5 text-[14px]\"><li><a class=\"text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline\" href=\"/peptide-research/how-to-verify-a-peptide-coa\">How to Verify a Peptide COA in Three Steps<!-- --> →</a></li><li><a class=\"text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline\" href=\"/peptide-research/how-to-spot-a-fake-coa\">How to Spot a Fake Peptide COA: Seven Red Flags<!-- --> →</a></li><li><a class=\"text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline\" href=\"/peptide-research/how-to-read-a-certificate-of-analysis\">How to Read a Certificate of Analysis<!-- --> →</a></li><li><a class=\"text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline\" href=\"/peptide-research/purity-vs-fill-accuracy\">Purity vs Fill Accuracy<!-- --> →</a></li><li><a class=\"text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline\" href=\"/peptide-research/janoshik-testing-explained\">Janoshik Testing Explained<!-- --> →</a></li></ul><h2 class=\"mt-12 text-xl font-semibold text-foreground\">Frequently asked questions</h2><dl class=\"mt-4 space-y-6\"><div><dt class=\"text-[14px] font-medium text-foreground\">What is a certificate of analysis (COA)?</dt><dd class=\"mt-2 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">A document issued by an analytical laboratory reporting what a specific production lot actually contains: identity (mass spectrometry), purity (HPLC), and ideally the measured quantity against the label. It is per-lot — a COA for last year’s batch says nothing about this year’s.</dd></div><div><dt class=\"text-[14px] font-medium text-foreground\">How do I verify an Eppix Labs batch?</dt><dd class=\"mt-2 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">Enter the lot code from your vial in the batch verifier, or find it in the COA library. Every published lot page carries the analytical figures and a link to the issuing laboratory’s own verification record, so the numbers can be checked outside our website.</dd></div><div><dt class=\"text-[14px] font-medium text-foreground\">Can a COA be faked?</dt><dd class=\"mt-2 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">A PDF can. That is why the load-bearing step is checking the result on the laboratory’s own portal rather than trusting the vendor-hosted copy — and why a vendor whose certificates cannot be looked up independently deserves skepticism regardless of what the numbers say.</dd></div></dl></div></section></div><!--$--><!--/$--></main><div class=\"no-overflow-x\"><footer class=\"glass\"><div class=\"border-b border-white/30 dark:border-border\"><ul class=\"mx-auto grid max-w-7xl grid-cols-1 gap-x-8 gap-y-1.5 px-4 py-4 sm:grid-cols-2 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-4 text-[12.5px] text-foreground-secondary\"><li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\"><span class=\"mt-[7px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>Independent lab report published for every lot</li><li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\"><span class=\"mt-[7px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>99.48% mean HPLC purity, all lots</li><li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\"><span class=\"mt-[7px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>Same-day dispatch before 4 pm · Xpresspost 1–2 days</li><li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\"><span class=\"mt-[7px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>Free shipping over $200 · Mix &amp; Match up to 25%</li></ul></div><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-14\"><div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 gap-y-10 gap-x-6 sm:gap-x-10 lg:grid-cols-6 lg:gap-x-10\"><div class=\"col-span-2 lg:col-span-2\"><a class=\"inline-block\" href=\"/\">